---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Pradipta" description="The experiences and beliefs behind Pradipta Das Sarkar’s approach to design leadership.">
  <section class="about-hero shell">
    <div class="about-hero-copy" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>I design complex systems. I find perspective beyond them.</h1>
      <p class="hero-body">I’m Pradipta—a design leader shaped by architecture, systems thinking, curiosity, and nearly two decades of learning how people make consequential decisions.</p>
      <ul class="about-interests" aria-label="Personal interests">
        <li><span>01</span> Mountains</li>
        <li><span>02</span> Long drives</li>
        <li><span>03</span> Photography</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <aside class="about-hero-aside" data-reveal>
      <figure class="about-hero-photo">
        <img src="/images/langza-monastery-spiti-valley.webp" width="1400" height="1650" alt="The Langza Buddha beneath the Milky Way in Spiti Valley">
        <figcaption>
          <div class="about-photo-credit"><span>Captured at</span><strong>Langza</strong><small>Spiti Valley · India</small></div>
          <ol class="about-photo-lessons">
            <li><span>01</span><p><strong>Architecture</strong> taught me structure.</p></li>
            <li><span>02</span><p><strong>Travel</strong> taught me perspective.</p></li>
            <li><span>03</span><p><strong>Photography</strong> taught me to notice.</p></li>
          </ol>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="evidence-section shell" data-reveal>
    <header class="evidence-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The evidence behind the practice</p><h2>Built through craft. Multiplied through people.</h2><p>My value is not one role, credential or award. It is the ability to connect design judgment, organizational scale and the energy to move an idea forward.</p></header>
    <div class="evidence-mosaic">
      <figure class="evidence-tile evidence-portrait"><img src="/images/profile-photo.webp" width="500" height="500" alt="Pradipta Das Sarkar"><figcaption>Designer. Builder. Leader.</figcaption></figure>
      <article class="evidence-tile evidence-number evidence-number-cyan"><strong>19</strong><p>years turning complex systems into understandable decisions</p></article>
      <article class="evidence-tile evidence-number evidence-number-blue"><strong>46+</strong><p>designers hired—and stronger teams built around them</p></article>
      <figure class="evidence-tile evidence-cooper"><img src="/images/cooper-facilitation-certificate.webp" width="800" height="787" alt="Cooper Professional Education certification in Facilitating Design Thinking"><figcaption><strong>Certified facilitator</strong><span>Equipped to lead design-thinking sessions with leaders and design teams.</span></figcaption></figure>

      <article class="evidence-tile evidence-education"><p class="eyebrow">Learning that compounds</p><ul><li><strong>Jadavpur University</strong><span>Architecture</span></li><li><strong>IIT Bombay</strong><span>Visual Communication</span></li><li><strong>IIM Bangalore</strong><span>Executive Education</span></li><li><strong>Cooper Professional Education</strong><span>Facilitating Design Thinking</span></li></ul></article>
      <figure class="evidence-tile evidence-workshop"><img src="/images/leadership-workshop-06.webp" width="1024" height="768" alt="Pradipta collaborating with colleagues during a design-thinking workshop"><figcaption><strong>Leadership in the room</strong><span>Creating the conditions for teams to think together.</span></figcaption></figure>

      <a class="evidence-tile evidence-artifact evidence-letter" href="/images/chuck-robbins-letter.webp" target="_blank" aria-label="Open the recognition letter from Chuck Robbins in a new tab"><img src="/images/chuck-robbins-letter.webp" width="1400" height="1256" alt="Recognition letter from Cisco Chairman and CEO Chuck Robbins"><span><strong>Recognition from Chuck Robbins</strong><small>For winning Cisco’s Innovate Everywhere Challenge 5 with Rule Heartbeat.</small><em>Open letter ↗</em></span></a>
      <figure class="evidence-tile evidence-trophy"><img src="/images/innovation-trophy.webp" width="675" height="900" alt="2020 Innovate Everywhere Challenge winner trophy for Rule Heartbeat"><figcaption><strong>2020 Winner</strong><span>Rule Heartbeat · Innovate Everywhere Challenge</span></figcaption></figure>
      <a class="evidence-tile evidence-artifact evidence-interview" href="/images/cisco-innovators-interview.webp" target="_blank" aria-label="Open the Cisco Innovators on Innovating interview in a new tab"><img src="/images/cisco-innovators-interview.webp" width="1600" height="1087" alt="Cisco Employee Connection interview titled Innovators on Innovating: Pradipta Das Sarkar"><span><strong>A story worth sharing</strong><small>Featured in Cisco’s global employee newsletter.</small><em>Open interview ↗</em></span></a>
      <figure class="evidence-tile evidence-workshop-story"><img src="/images/workshop-shared-model.webp" width="1400" height="933" alt="A workshop participant explaining a systems model to a colleague"><figcaption><span>Listen before leading</span><strong>Make every perspective visible.</strong></figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="evidence-tile evidence-workshop-story"><img src="/images/workshop-ideators.webp" width="1400" height="1120" alt="The Ideators team collaborating around workshop materials and sticky notes"><figcaption><span>Build shared ownership</span><strong>Move from individual ideas to collective direction.</strong></figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="evidence-tile evidence-workshop-room"><img src="/images/workshop-room-10.webp" width="1800" height="831" alt="A full room of participants collaborating during a facilitated design-thinking workshop"><figcaption><span>Facilitation at scale</span><strong>A room becomes a working system when every person can contribute.</strong></figcaption></figure>
      <article class="evidence-tile evidence-number evidence-number-coral evidence-workshop-count"><strong>30+</strong><p>design-thinking workshops facilitated with leaders and cross-functional teams</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-values" aria-label="Leadership values"><div><span>01</span><strong>Clarity</strong><p>Make complicated systems and decisions legible.</p></div><div><span>02</span><strong>Scale</strong><p>Build capabilities that continue beyond one person.</p></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Momentum</strong><p>Turn evidence and conviction into meaningful action.</p></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section shell" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow">01 · The foundation</p>
    <div><h2>I graduated in architecture. It trained me to see systems before screens.</h2><p>Architecture taught me that every visible outcome is held together by invisible decisions: structure, sequence, movement, constraint and context. That lens continues to shape how I approach enterprise products today.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="passion-feature shell" data-reveal>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">02 · The open road</p><h2>I gravitate toward places, moments and rituals that make life feel a little more awake.</h2><p>Travel gives me perspective. Photography sharpens attention. Long drives clear the noise. These are not escapes from design—they are how I return to it with a better frame.</p></div>
    <div class="open-road-gallery">
      <figure class="open-road-main"><img src="/images/open-road-snow.webp" width="1600" height="1045" alt="Pradipta standing beside his Duster during snowfall on a mountain road"><figcaption>Driving toward the view—even when the weather has other plans.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="open-road-secondary"><img src="/images/open-road-family.webp" width="1152" height="532" alt="Pradipta and his family beside their Duster on a road through Spiti Valley"><figcaption><span>Spiti Valley</span><strong>The road is part of the story.</strong></figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="personal-energy shell" data-reveal>
    <header><p class="eyebrow">03 · Personal energy</p><h2>Some of my best thinking happens away from the screen.</h2><p>Campfires, changing weather, road trips and time with family reset the system. They create enough distance for unfinished ideas to reorganise themselves.</p></header>
    <div class="personal-energy-photos">
      <figure><img src="/images/personal-energy-camp-cooking.webp" width="900" height="1234" alt="Pradipta and his family cooking together outdoors in the mountains" loading="lazy"></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/personal-energy-campfire.webp" width="900" height="1245" alt="Pradipta and his family gathered around a campfire in a forest" loading="lazy"></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/personal-energy-open-road.webp" width="900" height="1197" alt="Pradipta and his son sitting beside their Duster on a mountain road" loading="lazy"></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="landscape-story shell" data-reveal>
    <header><p class="eyebrow">04 · Places I remember</p><h2>I like landscapes that make you quiet for a minute.</h2><p>These are less about destinations and more about what they do to attention. They slow things down. They make composition obvious. They remind me that clarity is often about subtraction.</p></header>
    <div class="landscape-photos">
      <figure><img src="/images/landscape-buddha.webp" width="1000" height="663" alt="A seated Buddha overlooking a Himalayan valley" loading="lazy"></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/landscape-monastery.webp" width="1000" height="660" alt="A monastery built into a mountain valley beneath a vivid blue sky" loading="lazy"></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/landscape-sunset.webp" width="1000" height="556" alt="Himalayan peaks beneath dramatic golden clouds" loading="lazy"></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/landscape-stupa.webp" width="1000" height="647" alt="A white Buddhist stupa against mountains and a deep blue sky" loading="lazy"></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/landscape-camels.webp" width="1000" height="644" alt="A camel caravan reflected in still water beneath the mountains" loading="lazy"></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/landscape-lake.webp" width="1000" height="542" alt="A turquoise mountain lake surrounded by dark Himalayan ridges" loading="lazy"></figure>
      <figure class="landscape-night"><img src="/images/landscape-milky-way.webp" width="1800" height="653" alt="The Milky Way stretching across a dark night sky" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Langza after dark—when scale becomes impossible to ignore.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cricket-story shell" data-reveal>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">05 · Cricket</p><h2>I take my curiosity seriously—but not myself too seriously.</h2><p>I enjoy meeting people, cheering loudly, carrying too much camera enthusiasm on trips, and occasionally becoming the person who says, “Wait, this would make a good frame.” Cricket brings all of that together: energy, people, observation and pure joy.</p></div>
    <img src="/images/about-cricket.webp" width="1690" height="1510" alt="Pradipta celebrating Indian cricket with supporters and holding the Indian flag with a friend inside a cricket stadium" loading="lazy">
  </section>

  <section class="story-section story-dark shell" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow">06 · Leadership</p>
    <div><h2>Some of my best thinking happens away from the screen.</h2><p>Teams rarely need a leader with every answer. They need someone who can make the problem legible, create the conditions for good judgment, and know when to step back.</p><a class="button" href="/pradipta-resume-2026.pdf" target="_blank">Read my resume <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
